    "slot_key": "Training content for day-one usability",
    "slot_value": "Very short, task-focused training on how to read provenance, confidence, timestamps, and conflict indicators, plus examples of when to trust an output versus when to verify it. Users should be taught to trust an output when the data is recent, the provenance is from a known high-quality source, the confidence is high, and the indicators all agree. They should verify it when the timestamp is stale, the source is weak or missing, confidence is low, or there’s a conflict between vehicle, roadway, weather, and traveler signals. Main exception cases to emphasize are incidents, rapidly changing winter weather, and sensor outages, because outputs can become wrong very quickly in those situations. If a conflict affects a safety or operational action, users should verify before acting.",
    "operation": "refine"
